from pathlib import Path
import json,html
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((R/'SUMMARY.json').read_text())
rows=''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(v))+'</td>' for v in [r['mode'],r['scenario'],r['admitted'],r['flags'],round(r['medianW'],2),r['status']])+'</tr>' for r in s['results'])
doc='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Token pipeline qualification</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:40px auto;padding:20px;background:#f8faf7;color:#173c30}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #c5d4c9;text-align:left}table{border-collapse:collapse}</style><h1>Full synthetic token pipeline: '''+s['status']+'''</h1>
<p>Frozen before200fresh raw-token layouts and800outcomes. The path exercised is raw synthetic transcription → atlas-policy token cleaning → exact line/position eligibility → body matching → availability-pattern conditioning → W support → exact score. No manuscript files were read; H/F remain separate.</p>
<table><tr><th>Layout</th><th>Scenario</th><th>Admitted/100</th><th>Flags among admitted</th><th>Median W</th><th>Gate</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table>
<p>Dense fixtures encode known mixed-availability group designs with W≈166.286. Their extracted support must match the designed value. Sparse fixtures add0–3tokens at either end, replace20%of target origins with ordinary tokens and introduce5%unknown slots. These alter line lengths, positions and matching support without allowing renumbering or cross-line matching.</p>
<h2>Verification</h2><p>Every generated raw line is reparsed and checked against its intended tokens. Production eligibility is compared with an independent loop. Comma-adjacent uncertainty, brace annotations, exclamation marks, unknown slots, terminal markers and comments have explicit fixtures. Separate alternative word-boundary fixtures remain distinct. This is not real H/F alignment validation.</p>
<p>First/final origins and origins followed by unknown tokens are excluded. Unknown slots stay in source lengths and positions; gaps are never bridged. Structural chx followers cannot be qok and contribute no available support. Replacing outcome words leaves selected groups and W unchanged. Exact small subset distributions were checked by enumeration; full dense support independently matches the generator.</p>
<p>The W≥160 rule,8-page minimum and25%concentration limit are unchanged. All low-support cases abstain from the primary test. Diagnostic p-values are saved separately to reveal failures, but are not interpreted as qualified results. Unsupported sparse controls are not evidence that an association is absent.</p>
<p>Null gates require upper Wilson95≤.10; positive lower bound≥.80 for a15-point difference among available followers. Dense cells need100admitted trials; sparse cells need at least50. No admissions means sparse qualification is unsupported, regardless of diagnostic rejection counts.</p>
<p>Coverage remains limited to authored synthetic spelling and layout. This does not prove a full historical parser, validate inferred structural availability, or show that Voynich panels can meet support. H/F shared-locus alignment was not run. No thresholds or masks changed after outcomes. Every failure and unsupported layout remains available.</p>
<p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen rules</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Hashes</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.json">Results and intervals</a> · <a href="DESIGNS.json">Raw synthetic lines and support</a> · <a href="TRIALS.json">All outcomes</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification</a></p>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(doc,encoding='utf-8')
assert all((R/f).exists() for f in ['PROTOCOL.json','FREEZE.json','SUMMARY.json','DESIGNS.json','TRIALS.json','VERIFICATION.json'])
print(json.dumps(s,indent=2))
